    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high offensive output today, anchored by the elite 81.88 efficiency rating of **Gunnar Henderson**. Facing the vulnerable arm of Curry (xERA 5.68), **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an optimal #3 spot in the order and a massive +19% SP skill advantage. He is joined in the \"Strong\" start tier by **Kyle Tucker** (75.28) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.84). **Kyle Tucker** overcomes a neutral platoon against Abbott to provide immense value, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a significant +14% dynamic platoon edge against Matthews. Furthermore, **Jackson Merrill** remains a high-upside play at 71.56, bolstered by a +14% park factor, proving he is a foundational piece against the Adams matchup. \n\n**Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.91) rounds out our primary threats, though we are keeping a close eye on **Drake Baldwin** (56.70) and **Coby Mayo** (52.76), who occupy the \"Marginal\" start category. While **Coby Mayo** faces a favorable 5.68 xERA pitcher, his ceiling is slightly capped by a negative dynamic platoon hit of -8%. Our most difficult bench decision was opting to sit **Miguel Vargas** (47.59) in favor of higher-floor starters. While **Miguel Vargas** showed promising xwOBA metrics, the combination of Messick\u2019s respectable 3.54 xERA and the overall depth of the starting nine made him the odd man out. We also continue to monitor the status of **Andy Pages** and **Jordan Westburg**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us to navigate the thin margins of our current active roster. With **Nasim Nunez** falling below our 40.0 efficiency floor due to a poor matchup against Wheeler and a lower-order lineup spot, we are strictly prioritizing the high-ceiling production of our primary starters to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings.",
